DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261020T181500
SUMMARY:💬 Drama: Ali Imsirovic: Player of the Year to a $320\,000 seizure (partial confession)
DESCRIPTION:Status: SCHEDULED on X (seen in Poker Poster's scheduled queue)\nClip slug: drama-09\nClip status: render NOT found on box\nPost text (as scheduled on X):\nIn 2021\, Ali Imsirovic was named poker's Player of the Year. Two years later\, he admitted multi-accounting\, a form of online poker cheating\, and said $320\,000 had been seized from him.\n\nImsirovic rose fast. He won the Poker Masters in 2018\, then spent the next years collecting big wins in the most expensive tournaments in the world.\n\nIn April 2022\, other high-stakes players said he had been banned by the online site GGPoker. The accusations included multi-accounting\, ghosting and real-time assistance.\n\nIn plain words: multi-accounting means entering the same tournament under several names\, so you get extra chances to win. Ghosting means someone secretly makes decisions for another player. Real-time assistance means software that tells you the best move while you play.\n\nHe stayed silent for more than a year\, and was barred from PokerGO's tournaments.\n\nIn June 2023 he posted a 30-minute video. He admitted multi-accounting\, confirmed the GGPoker ban and said the site seized $320\,000. He also admitted going back to it briefly after he had been caught.\n\n"I have multi-accounted a bunch\, so I have no interest in denying that. It happened. I regret it\, but it happened\," he said.\n\nBut he firmly denied using real-time assistance or ghosting\, and rejected other accusations against him. Much of the poker world reacted badly\, feeling he spent more time on what he didn't do than on what he did.\n\nThat is the strange power of a partial confession. Admitting one thing can make your other denials sound more believable. It can also make people wonder what else you haven't admitted.\n\nWhen someone admits part of what they're accused of\, do you trust their denials more\, or less?\nNote: replies on this post must never state allegations as fact\; attach Clip Lab key-moment clip if ready before slot
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
