SUMMARY:💬 Drama: Mike Postle (approved as written)
DESCRIPTION:Status: SCHEDULED on X (seen in Poker Poster's scheduled queue)\nClip slug: drama-07\nClip status: render NOT found on box\nPost text (as scheduled on X):\nA poker player won an estimated $250\,000 in livestreamed games at a small California casino. Regulars nicknamed him "God". Then a commentator suggested he might be cheating.\n\nFrom July 2018\, Mike Postle went on a remarkable run in low-stakes games streamed from Stones Gambling Hall near Sacramento. He made strange decisions that kept working: folding strong hands just before they lost\, staying in with weak ones just before they won.\n\nThe stream showed viewers every player's face-down cards\, read by sensors in the table\, on a 30-minute delay.\n\nOn September 21\, 2019\, Postle folded a strong hand against an opponent holding the best possible hand. Commentator Veronica Brill said on air: "It's like he knows."\n\nA week later she posted a video of his hands. "Am I sure that this player is cheating? No\," she wrote. But she believed he might be secretly receiving card information.\n\nOthers studied hours of footage and found it suspicious. Postle denied cheating\, said his winnings were overstated and described his style as deliberately unpredictable. "There aren't words to describe what I do\," he said on a podcast.\n\n88 players sued him and the casino for $30 million. In 2020\, a judge dismissed the claims against Postle because California law generally bars suing to recover gambling losses. It was not a ruling on whether he cheated. Postle then filed a $330 million defamation suit against his accusers\, and dropped it in 2021.\n\nNo court has ever found that he cheated. No one has ever explained how he could have.\n\nThe idea: results alone can raise a question. They cannot answer it.\n\nHow much evidence would you need before publicly accusing someone of cheating?\nNote: HIGH defamation risk: never write that Postle cheated anywhere\, including replies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
